  "weakest_point": "The twenty-first primitive boundary now covers the generic prim_clock_gating path, but the active primitive set still has no direct onehot/control-integrity checker claim. A prim_onehot_check gate can target AddrWidth=3, OneHotWidth=8, AddrCheck=1, EnableCheck=1, StrictCheck=1, and EnableAlertTriggerSVA=0 while keeping all widths, disabled check modes, alert-trigger SVA integration, full security countermeasure proof, raw full-state equality, and zero-initialized GPU correctness outside the claim.",
  "why_this_target": [
    "the twenty-first primitive review accepted prim_clock_gating while leaving onehot/control-integrity checking outside the active claim",
    "prim_onehot_check is a source-backed OpenTitan primitive with a concrete binary-tree check path",
    "fixed AddrWidth=3 and OneHotWidth=8 keep the next gate narrower than broad alert/esc differential signaling or arbiter-tree families",
    "enabled address, enable, and strict checks add more claim value than a standalone pass-through wrapper",
    "disabling the alert-trigger SVA integration keeps the gate focused on coverage-output behavior instead of a broader security assertion proof"
  ],
  "rejected_for_now": [
